## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary: 13 findings — 8 Critical, 3 Medium, 2 Low

This test suite is a **textbook coverage-touching class**. All 10 public methods on `ProductCatalog` are called, achieving high line coverage, but almost nothing is actually verified. 5 of 10 tests have **zero assertions**; the other 5 use only `Assert.IsNotNull`, which is trivially weak. This explains why bugs escape to production despite 95% coverage.

---

### 🔴 Critical — Tests Giving False Confidence

**1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (systemic, all 10 tests)**
Every public method is called in declaration order with no meaningful verification. This is the single biggest problem — the entire suite exists to inflate coverage metrics.

**2. No Assertions — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17–21)**
Calls `AddProduct` but never verifies the product was stored.
```csharp
// FIX:
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}
```

**3. No Assertions — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 31–36)**
Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price changed.
```csharp
// FIX:
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesProductPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
}
```

**4. No Assertions — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38–43)**
Product is removed but never verified as absent.
```csharp
// FIX:
[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_MakesProductUnretrievable()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}
```

**5. No Assertions — `GetProductCount_Works` (line 62–66)**
Gets the count and discards it.
```csharp
// FIX:
[TestMethod]
public void GetProductCount_ReturnsCorrectCount()
{
    Assert.AreEqual(0, _catalog.GetProductCount());
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());
}
```

**6. No Assertions — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68–74)**
Applies a 10% discount but never checks any price changed. A bug in the discount formula (e.g. `p.Price * fraction` instead of `p.Price * (1 - fraction)`) would pass.
